# Knowledge Store Skill

Captures URLs, articles, Slack forwards, and free-text notes into CUGA's knowledge base.
Stored content is available for querying and for the bulletin skill to synthesize.

## What this skill does

- Detects URLs in the user's message and ingests the page content via `ingest_knowledge_url`
- Accepts plain text notes: write the text to `/tmp/cuga-note-<slug>.md`, then call `ingest_knowledge` with that file path and `scope="agent"`
- Always uses `scope="agent"` so content persists across sessions
- Confirms each storage with a one-line summary

## Handling plain text (no URL)

When the user provides a text snippet to store and no URL is present:
1. Use the code executor to write the text to `/tmp/cuga-note-<short-slug>.md`
2. Call `ingest_knowledge(file_path="/tmp/cuga-note-<short-slug>.md", scope="agent")`
3. Confirm with one line: "Stored: [brief description]"

Do NOT refuse plain-text input. Do NOT ask for a URL. Always write text to a temp file and ingest it.

## Usage examples

- Forward a link: `store this as a v3.4 feature` + URL → calls `ingest_knowledge_url`
- Save a note: `/store We shipped async exports — reduces wait time by 80%` → writes temp file, calls `ingest_knowledge`
- Save an article: `/remember https://example.com/article` → calls `ingest_knowledge_url`
